use web
use json
use core
use md
into picker.he
lang he

The module is namespace `picker`. It owns the composer bar under the chat input, the model picker dialog, offline mode, the welcome status card and the keyboard shortcuts sheet of the Amni-Code page. Its tags are 600 to 699. A web element handle of 0 means the element does not exist, and every web call given 0 does nothing. Generated HTML is built into growable byte buffers named `h`. Every dynamic text placed in generated HTML goes through `md::esc`, which appends the escaped text to a buffer. Generated HTML never has inline handlers; buttons and links carry "data-act" attributes that the root program routes to `act`. Elements are found by id with `web::el` and by selector with `web::query` under `web::DOCUMENT`. Classes are changed with `web::cls` and `web::has_cls`.

The tags are i32 constants: `KEYS` 600, `CLICKS` 601, `CFG_FULL` 602, `CFG_PART` 603, `PROVS` 604, `SERVERS` 605, `MODELS` 607, `SAVE_PLAIN` 608, `SAVE_MODE` 609, `SAVE_USE` 610, `SAVE_OFFLINE` 611, `FOCUS` 612, `CHANGED` 613, `DELAY` 614, `FILTER` 615, `OFFCHECK` 617, `SHEET` 618.

Module state is held in json documents and byte buffers. `cfg_doc` with the int `cfg_root` (starting at -1) holds the last good response of the config endpoint, an object. `prov_doc` with `prov_root` (starting at -1) holds the last good response of the providers endpoint, an object with the array "providers" and the array "suggested_local". `srv_doc` with `srv_root` (starting at -1) holds the last response of the local servers endpoint, an object with the array "servers"; a root of -1 means there are no servers. `mod_doc` with `mod_root` (starting at -1) holds the last good response of the models endpoint, an object with the array "models" and the strings "source" and "error". `scratch` is one more document used only for checking. `pend_mode`, `pend_provider` and `pend_model` are byte buffers and `pend_on` is a bool; they remember what the save request in flight asked for.

`adopt(text, d, root)` takes a json text, a document `d` and an int `root`, both passed by reference. It first parses `text` into `scratch` with `json::parse`. When that gives a root of 0 or more, it parses `text` into `d` again with `json::parse`, stores that root in `root` and returns true. Otherwise it changes nothing and returns false.

`take_json(d, root)` is called while a fetch event is being handled. It reads the response body for `web::ev_id()` with `web::fetch_take` into a local growable buffer, then calls `web::fetch_free` for it. It returns true when `web::ev_status()` is from 200 to 299 and `adopt` of the body into `d` and `root` succeeds, otherwise false.

`field(d, n, key)` returns the text of the string member `key` of object node `n` in document `d`, or an empty string when `n` is negative, the member is missing or it is not a string. `flag(d, n, key)` returns true only when that member is the json value true.

`cfg_str(key)` is `field` of `cfg_doc` at `cfg_root`. `cfg_on(key)` is `flag` of `cfg_doc` at `cfg_root`.

`provider_node(id)` returns the element of the "providers" array of `prov_doc` (the member of `prov_root`) whose "id" string equals `id`, or -1 when there is none. `is_cloud(id)` is true when `provider_node(id)` has its "cloud" flag true.

`up_count()` is the number of elements of the "servers" array of `srv_doc` (the member of `srv_root`) whose "up" flag is true.

`label_of(out, id)` appends the display name of a provider id: "amni" gives "Adam", "ollama" gives "Ollama", "local" gives "Local", "openai" gives "OpenAI", "anthropic" gives "Anthropic", "google" gives "Gemini", "xai" gives "xAI", and any other id is appended unchanged.

`model_or(out, model, fallback)` appends `core::model_label` of `model`; when that appends nothing it appends `fallback` instead.

`core_models(id)` returns the node of the member "models" of `core::provider(id)` inside the document `core::tables`, or -1 when there is none.

`matches(q, s)` is true when `q` is empty, or when the lowercase of `s` (std `lower`) contains `q`.

`add_row(h, provider, model, base, disabled, title, badge)` appends one picker model row. It is active when `cfg_str("provider")` equals `provider` and `cfg_str("model")` equals `model`. The row is `<button type="button" class="pk-row` then ` active` when active, then `" data-act="picker.use" data-provider="` PROVIDER `" data-model="` MODEL `" data-base="` BASE `"` then ` disabled` when `disabled`, then ` title="` TITLE `">` where TITLE is `title`, or `model` when `title` is empty. Then `<span class="pk-name">` followed by `core::model_label` of the model, escaped, then `</span><span class="pk-meta"></span>`, then when `badge` is not empty `<span class="pk-badge ok">` BADGE `</span>`, then when active `<span class="pk-check">✓</span>`, then `</button>`. PROVIDER, MODEL, BASE, TITLE and BADGE are escaped.

`rows_of(h, d, arr, provider, base, disabled, title, badge, q, limit)` appends model rows for the string elements of the array node `arr` in json document `d`. Elements that are not strings, and elements that do not `matches` `q`, are skipped. Every other element calls `add_row` with `h`, `provider`, the element's string, `base`, `disabled`, `title` and `badge`. When `limit` is above 0 it stops after `limit` rows.

`filter_text(out)` appends the lowercase of the "value" property of the element "pk-filter" (`web::el`, `web::get_prop`), nothing when the element does not exist, and then releases that element's handle with `web::release`.

`servers_html(h, q)` appends the local section. First `<div class="pk-sec">Local · works offline</div>`. When the "servers" array of `srv_doc` has no elements it appends `<div class="pk-note">Scanning for local servers…</div>`. Then for each element `s` of that array, with `up` being its "up" flag, it appends `<div class="pk-srv ` then "up" or "down", then `"><span class="ab-dot ` then "local" when up else "off", then `"></span><span>` the escaped "label" `</span><span class="pk-url">` the escaped "base_url" with its first "http://" removed `</span><span class="pk-state">` then, when up, the number of elements of its "models" array followed by ` model` and an "s" unless that number is 1, or, when not up, `not running`, then `</span></div>`. When up it then adds model rows through `rows_of` for the elements of its "models" array in `srv_doc`, with provider the server's "provider", base the server's "base_url", not disabled, an empty title, badge "offline" and no limit; but when that "models" array has no elements and the server's "provider" is "amni", it instead adds the two rows "adam:3b" and "adam:8b" through `add_row` with the same arguments, each only when it `matches` `q`. After the loop, when the "servers" array has elements and `up_count()` is 0, it appends `<div class="pk-note">No local model server is running. Start Adam (Amni-AI, :7700) or <code>ollama serve</code> (:11434).</div>`.

`suggested_html(h)` appends `<div class="pk-sec">Suggested local models</div>` then, for each element `m` of the "suggested_local" array of `prov_doc`, `<div class="pk-sugg"><div class="pk-sugg-t"><b>` the escaped "label" `</b><span class="pk-meta">` the integer part of the "context" number divided by 1024.0 `K context · ` the escaped "gguf" `</span></div><div class="pk-cmd"><code>ollama pull ` the escaped "ollama" `</code><button type="button" class="pk-copy" data-act="picker.copy" data-arg="ollama pull ` the escaped "ollama" `">Copy</button><button type="button" class="pk-use" data-act="picker.use" data-provider="ollama" data-model="` the escaped "ollama" `" data-base="http://127.0.0.1:11434">Use</button></div></div>`.

`cloud_html(h, q)` appends the cloud section. First `<div class="pk-sec">Cloud · needs a key and internet</div>`. Then for each id in the order "anthropic", "openai", "google", "xai": let `pr` be `provider_node(id)`, and skip the id when it is -1. Let `blocked` be `cfg_on("offline")`. Append `<div class="pk-prov">` then the escaped "label" of `pr` in `prov_doc`, then ` <span class="pk-badge ok">key found</span>` when its "has_env_key" flag is true, then ` <span class="pk-badge warn">off while offline</span>` when `blocked`, then `</div>`. Then append model rows with provider `id`, base the "default_base" of `pr`, disabled `blocked`, title "Turn Offline mode off to use cloud models" when `blocked` else empty, no badge and limit 8, taking the models from the first source that applies: first, when `cfg_str("provider")` equals `id` and the "models" array of `mod_doc` has at least one element, that array through `rows_of`; second, when `core_models(id)` has at least one element, that array in `core::tables` through `rows_of`; otherwise a single row for the "default_model" string of `pr`, through `add_row`, only when that string is not empty and `matches` `q`.

`render_picker()` does nothing when the element "amni-picker" does not exist. Otherwise it reads the filter text `q` with `filter_text`, then builds `h` from, in order: `<div class="pk-head"><input id="pk-filter" placeholder="Filter models…" value="` then `q` escaped then `" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Filter models"><button type="button" class="pk-close" data-act="picker.close" title="Close (Esc)">✕</button></div><div class="pk-body">`; `servers_html(h, q)`; `suggested_html(h)`; `cloud_html(h, q)`; then `<div class="pk-foot">`; then, only when the "source" string of `mod_doc` is not empty, the text `Model list: ` followed by that string escaped (when the source is empty nothing at all is appended for it, not even `Model list: `); then, only when the "error" string of `mod_doc` is not empty, ` (` followed by that string escaped and `)`; then ` · <a href="#" data-act="picker.settings">All providers and keys</a></div></div>`. It sets the HTML of "amni-picker" to `h` with `web::html`, then listens on the new element "pk-filter" for "input" with tag `FILTER` and no flags.

`filter_input()` handles an input event of the filter field. It reads the "selectionStart" number of `web::ev_target()` with `web::get_num`, calls `render_picker()`, then finds "pk-filter", focuses it with `web::call` and the method "focus", and sets its "selectionStart" and then its "selectionEnd" properties to the saved number with `web::prop_num`.

`open_picker()` finds the element "amni-picker"; when none exists it creates a div with id "amni-picker", class "amni-picker", attribute "role" "dialog" and attribute "aria-label" "Choose a model" and appends it to `web::BODY`. It adds the class "open" to it, calls `render_picker()`, calls `refresh(true)` and starts a 30 millisecond `web::timer` with tag `FOCUS`. `close_picker()` removes the class "open" of "amni-picker". `toggle_picker()` calls `close_picker()` when "amni-picker" exists and has the class "open", otherwise `open_picker()`.

`ensure_bar()` returns the handle of the element "amni-bar" when it exists. Otherwise it finds the first element matching "#pane-0 .input-area" with `web::query`, or when there is none the first ".input-area", and returns 0 when there is neither. It creates a div with id "amni-bar" and class "amni-bar", sets its HTML to `<button type="button" class="ab-pill" id="ab-model" data-act="picker.toggle" title="Choose provider and model (Ctrl+K)" aria-haspopup="dialog"><span class="ab-dot"></span><span class="ab-prov"></span><span class="ab-model"></span><span class="ab-caret">▾</span></button><button type="button" class="ab-chip" id="ab-offline" data-act="picker.offline" title="Offline mode: local models only, no web tools (Ctrl+Shift+O)" aria-pressed="false"><span class="ab-led"></span><span class="ab-off-label">Online</span></button><div class="ab-mode" role="group" aria-label="Agent mode"><button type="button" data-act="picker.mode" data-arg="plan" data-mode="plan" title="Plan: propose, never change files">Plan</button><button type="button" data-act="picker.mode" data-arg="edit" data-mode="edit" title="Edit: apply changes">Edit</button><button type="button" data-act="picker.mode" data-arg="autonomous" data-mode="autonomous" title="Autonomous: run everything">Auto</button></div><span class="ab-spacer"></span><button type="button" class="ab-help" id="ab-help" data-act="picker.shortcuts" title="Keyboard shortcuts (?)">Shortcuts <kbd>?</kbd></button>`, appends it to the input area and returns it.

`render_welcome()` does nothing when the element "welcome" does not exist. It finds the element "amni-status-card"; when there is none it creates a div with that id and class "amni-status-card" and appends it to "welcome". It builds `h` from `<div class="sc-line">` followed by one of three texts. When the "servers" array of `srv_doc` has no elements: `<span class="ab-dot off"></span> Checking for local model servers…`. Otherwise, when `up_count()` is above 0: `<span class="ab-dot local"></span> Local model server`, then an "s" when `up_count()` is above 1, then `: `, then for each server whose "up" flag is true, in order and joined with ` · `, `<b>` the escaped "label" `</b> (` the number of elements of its "models" array `)`. Otherwise: `<span class="ab-dot off"></span> No local model server found. Start Adam (:7700) or Ollama (:11434), or <a href="#" data-act="picker.open">pick a cloud model</a>.`. Then it appends `</div><div class="sc-sub">Using <b>` then the escaped `label_of` of `cfg_str("provider")`, or "…" when the provider is empty, then `</b> · ` then the escaped `model_or` of `cfg_str("model")` with the fallback "no model", then ` · <span class="sc-off">offline</span>` when `cfg_on("offline")`, then ` · <a href="#" data-act="picker.open">change</a> <kbd>Ctrl</kbd><kbd>K</kbd></div>`. It sets the HTML of the card to `h`.

`render_settings_toggle()` does nothing when the element "cfg-provider" does not exist. When the element "cfg-offline-row" does not exist it creates a div with that id and class "cfg-offline-row", sets its HTML to `<label class="cfg-off-label"><input type="checkbox" id="cfg-offline"> Offline mode</label><p class="toggle-desc">Local models only. Cloud providers, web_search, web_fetch, model downloads and update checks are switched off, with a clear message instead of a timeout.</p>`, inserts it with `web::insert_before` into the parent of "cfg-provider" (`web::parent`) before the previous element sibling of "cfg-provider" (found with `web::js_get` and the path "previousElementSibling"), and listens on its new element "cfg-offline" for "change" with tag `OFFCHECK` and no flags. Finally it sets the "checked" property of "cfg-offline" to `cfg_on("offline")` with `web::prop_bool`.

`render()` does nothing when `ensure_bar()` gives 0 or `cfg_root` is negative. Let `provider` be `cfg_str("provider")`, `on` be `cfg_on("offline")`, `cloud` be `is_cloud(provider)`, and `seat` be true when the "providers" array of `prov_doc` has at least one element and `provider_node(provider)` is -1. Inside the bar it sets: the "class" attribute of the first ".ab-dot" to "ab-dot seat" when seat, else "ab-dot cloud" when cloud, else "ab-dot local"; the text of ".ab-prov" to `label_of` of the provider; the text of ".ab-model" to `model_or` of `cfg_str("model")` with the fallback "choose a model"; the class "on" of "#ab-offline" to `on`; its "aria-pressed" attribute to "true" when on else "false"; the text of its ".ab-off-label" to "Offline" when on else "Online"; for each button matching ".ab-mode button" (use `web::query_all` and `web::list_at` and read each button's "data-mode" attribute with `web::get_attr`, making no other query inside the loop), the class "on" to whether that attribute equals `cfg_str("mode")`, or "edit" when the mode is empty. It sets the class "amni-offline" of `web::BODY` to `on`. Let `warn` be `on` and `cloud`; it sets the class "warn" of the bar to `warn` and the "title" property of "#ab-model" to "Offline mode is on but a cloud provider is selected: pick a local model" when warn, else "Choose provider and model (Ctrl+K)". Then it calls `render_welcome()` and `render_settings_toggle()`, and calls `render_picker()` when `web::query` under `web::DOCUMENT` finds "#amni-picker.open".

`refresh(full)` starts `web::fetch` of "/api/config" with tag `CFG_FULL` when `full` is true, otherwise with tag `CFG_PART`.

`on_config(tag)` ends the chain when `take_json` of `cfg_doc` and `cfg_root` fails. Otherwise, when `tag` is `CFG_FULL` or the "providers" array of `prov_doc` has no elements, it starts `web::fetch` of "/api/providers" with tag `PROVS`; otherwise it starts `web::fetch` of "/api/models" with tag `MODELS`.

`on_providers()` calls `take_json` of `prov_doc` and `prov_root` and ignores the result, then starts `web::fetch` of "/api/local-servers" with tag `SERVERS`.

`on_servers()` calls `take_json` of `srv_doc` and `srv_root` and sets `srv_root` to -1 when it fails, then starts `web::fetch` of "/api/models" with tag `MODELS`.

`on_models()` calls `take_json` of `mod_doc` and `mod_root` and ignores the result, then calls `render()`.

`save_cfg(tag, body)` posts the text `body` to "/api/config" with `web::request`, method "POST", the headers text `{"Content-Type":"application/json"}`, the given tag and a timeout of 0.

`save_offline(on, tag)` stores `on` in `pend_on` and calls `save_cfg` with `tag` and the text `{"offline":` followed by `json::format_bool` of `on` and `}`.

`save_mode(mode)` replaces `pend_mode` with `mode` and calls `save_cfg` with tag `SAVE_MODE` and the text `{"mode":` followed by `json::format_string` of `mode` and `}`.

`save_use(provider, model, base)` replaces `pend_provider` with `provider` and `pend_model` with `model`, then calls `save_cfg` with tag `SAVE_USE` and the text `{"provider":` then `json::format_string` of the provider, `,"model":` then `json::format_string` of the model, then, only when `base` is not empty, `,"base_url":` then `json::format_string` of the base, then `}`.

`toggle_offline()` calls `save_offline` with the opposite of `cfg_on("offline")` and tag `SAVE_OFFLINE`.

`on_saved(tag)` ends a save request. It does nothing when `take_json` of `cfg_doc` and `cfg_root` fails. Otherwise it calls `core::post` with the action "settings.load" and an empty argument, then `render()`, then by tag. For `SAVE_MODE` it sets the "value" property of the element "cfg-mode" to `pend_mode` when that element exists. For `SAVE_USE`: when the element "cfg-model" exists, it looks through its "option" elements (`web::query_all` and `web::list_at`, comparing each "value" property read with `web::get_prop`, making no other query inside the loop) and, when none has the value `pend_model`, creates an option element with `web::create` whose "value" property and text are `pend_model` and appends it to "cfg-model"; then it sets the "value" property of "cfg-model" to `pend_model`. Still for `SAVE_USE`, it then calls `close_picker()`, then `core::toast` with the text "Using " followed by `label_of` of `pend_provider`, then " · ", then `core::model_label` of `pend_model`, then `refresh(false)`. For `SAVE_OFFLINE` it calls `core::toast` with "Offline mode on: cloud providers and web tools are disabled" when `pend_on` is true, otherwise "Offline mode off". `SAVE_PLAIN` does nothing more.

`show_shortcuts()` finds the element "amni-keys". When there is none it creates a div with id "amni-keys", class "amni-keys", attribute "role" "dialog" and attribute "aria-label" "Keyboard shortcuts"; it builds `h` from `<div class="ak-box"><div class="ak-head">Keyboard shortcuts<button type="button" class="pk-close" title="Close">✕</button></div>`, then for each shortcut, in order, `<div class="ak-row"><kbd>` KEY `</kbd><span>` DESCRIPTION `</span></div>` with both escaped, then `</div>`; it sets the HTML of the div to `h`, listens on it for "click" with tag `SHEET` and no flags, and appends it to `web::BODY`. The shortcuts as key and description pairs, in order, are: "Ctrl/⌘ K" "Choose provider and model"; "Ctrl/⌘ Shift O" "Toggle Offline mode"; "Ctrl/⌘ Shift L" "Toggle light / dark"; "Ctrl/⌘ Shift P" "Command palette"; "Ctrl/⌘ P" "Quick open file"; "Ctrl/⌘ ," "Settings"; "Ctrl/⌘ Shift N" "New chat"; "Enter · Shift Enter" "Send · new line"; "/" "Focus the prompt"; "?" "This list"; "Esc" "Close panels, stop generation". In every case it finally adds the class "open" to the element.

`sheet_click()` handles a click on the shortcuts sheet. It removes the class "open" of "amni-keys" when `web::same` says `web::ev_target()` is the sheet itself, or when `web::closest` of the target for ".pk-close" is not 0.

`typing(target)` is true when the "tagName" property of the element `target` (read with `web::get_prop`) is "INPUT", "TEXTAREA" or "SELECT", or when its "isContentEditable" property (`web::get_bool`) is true.

`on_key()` handles the document keydown event. It reads the key with `web::ev_key` and the modifiers with `web::ev_mods`. `mod` is true when `web::CTRL` or `web::META` is set, `shift` is true when `web::SHIFT` is set, and `k` is the key lowercased. The first matching case wins, in this order. Case 1: `mod`, not shift, and k is "k": call `web::ev_prevent()` and `toggle_picker()`. Case 2: `mod`, shift and k is "o": prevent default and `toggle_offline()`. Case 3: `mod`, shift and k is "l": prevent default and `core::post("look.tone", "")`. Case 4: `mod`, shift and k is "n": prevent default and click the element "new-chat" with `web::call` and the method "click". Case 5: `mod` and k is ",": prevent default and click the element "settings-btn". Case 6: the key itself (not lowercased) is "Escape": `close_picker()`, remove the class "open" of "amni-keys", and click the element "interrupt" when it exists and its "disabled" property (`web::get_bool`) is false; this case does not prevent default. Case 7: not `mod`, not `typing` of `web::ev_target()`, and the key is "?": prevent default and `show_shortcuts()`. Case 8: not `mod`, not `typing` of `web::ev_target()`, and the key is "/": prevent default and focus the element "input" with `web::call` and the method "focus".

`outside_click()` handles the document click event. It finds the element matching "#amni-picker.open" with `web::query` under `web::DOCUMENT`. When it exists, and `web::ev_target()` is not inside it (`web::contains`), has no closest ancestor matching "#ab-model" and no closest ancestor matching the selector [data-act='picker.open'] (`web::closest`), it calls `close_picker()`.

`act(verb, arg)` runs one queued action by verb. "open" calls `open_picker()`. "close" calls `close_picker()`. "toggle" calls `toggle_picker()`. "offline" calls `toggle_offline()`. "shortcuts" calls `show_shortcuts()`. "refresh" calls `refresh` with true when `arg` is "full", otherwise false. "settings" calls `close_picker()` and then clicks the element "settings-btn" with `web::call` and the method "click". "copy" calls `web::clipboard` with `arg` and sets the text of `core::act_el` to "Copied". "use" does nothing when the "disabled" property of `core::act_el` is true or its "data-provider" attribute is missing or empty; otherwise it calls `save_use` with the element's "data-provider", "data-model" and "data-base" attributes (read with `web::get_attr`, empty when missing). "mode" calls `save_mode` with `arg`. Any other verb is ignored.

`event(tag, kind)` dispatches by tag. `KEYS` calls `on_key()`. `CLICKS` calls `outside_click()`. `CHANGED` starts a 400 millisecond `web::timer` with tag `DELAY`. `DELAY` calls `refresh(false)`. `FOCUS` focuses the element "pk-filter" with `web::call` and the method "focus". `FILTER` calls `filter_input()`. `OFFCHECK` calls `save_offline` with `web::ev_checked()` and tag `SAVE_PLAIN`. `SHEET` calls `sheet_click()`. For the fetch tags, only when `kind` is `web::EV_FETCH`: `CFG_FULL` and `CFG_PART` call `on_config(tag)`, `PROVS` calls `on_providers()`, `SERVERS` calls `on_servers()`, `MODELS` calls `on_models()`, and `SAVE_PLAIN`, `SAVE_MODE`, `SAVE_USE` and `SAVE_OFFLINE` call `on_saved(tag)`. Other tags are ignored.

`init()` calls `ensure_bar()` and `refresh(true)`, listens on `web::DOCUMENT` for "keydown" with tag `KEYS` and for "click" with tag `CLICKS`, both with no flags, and, for each of the elements "cfg-provider" and "cfg-model" that exists, listens on it for "change" with tag `CHANGED` and no flags.
